# Disable ALL end-of-line conversion.
#
# The manifest stores a SHA-256 of each CSV's exact bytes. A clone with
# core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) rewrites LF to CRLF on checkout,
# which changes every byte, breaks every checksum, and makes mirror_fred.py
# --verify-all fail and --restore-all refuse. Verified 2026-08-03: converting
# NFCI.csv to CRLF produced "sha256 mismatch" and blocked the restore.
#
# The failure is fail-closed, so it cannot corrupt an archive -- but it would
# block recovery at exactly the moment recovery is needed.
* -text
*.csv -text
*.json -text
